Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
.vs/
*.sln

# Imported art — Fab, Megascans, anything with a licence on it.
#
# Fab's standard licence is per seat and per project: those assets may
# ship inside a packaged build and may NOT live in this repository (see
# the README's "High-end assets from Fab"). Importing a pack in the
# editor drops it straight into Content/, so without this the first
# `git status` after an import offers to commit the whole thing.
#
# Nothing is lost by ignoring it. The factory treats hero art as
# optional by design — no Content/, and every car builds the primitive
# shell it always did. Unanchored, so a plugin's own Content/ is caught
# too. scripts/check-structure.mjs fails if any of it is ever tracked,
# because an ignore rule does not un-track what is already committed.
Content/
*.uasset
*.umap

# macOS. Xcode workspaces and their derived data are generated from the
# .uproject by `unreal/mac/connect.sh` (or by right-clicking the project
# in Finder), so they are a build output like Binaries/ and Intermediate/
# and belong in the tree no more than those do.
*.xcworkspace
*.xcodeproj
DerivedData/
.DS_Store
